  "description": {
    "raw": "This spell strengthens the subject’s connection to the ground below, bolstering its defense against combat maneuvers. It gains a +2 insight bonus to its CMD to resist being moved or tripped and a +2 competence bonus on all Acrobatics checks made to balance or remain standing on earth, sand, stone, or a similar rocky substance.\n\nNote from Jason Bulmahn: The following spells are different from your standard cantrips. They are rare cantrips. Spellcasters that gain access to all 0-level spells at 1st level do not gain access to rare cantrips. A spellcaster gains access to rare cantrips only by uncovering their secrets in some other way. Some are guarded by jealous mages, while others are lost in missing libraries or molder on forgotten scrolls.\n\nThese cantrips are not legal in Pathfinder Society play. Note that penumbra was changed into the higher-level spell protective penumbra. The cantrip version is similar, but does not replace its higher-level counterpart.",
    "search_text": "\"this spell strengthens the subject’s connection to the ground below, bolstering its defense against combat maneuvers. it gains a +2 insight bonus to its cmd to resist being moved or tripped and a +2 competence bonus on all acrobatics checks made to balance or remain standing on earth, sand, stone, or a similar rocky substance.\\n\\nnote from jason bulmahn: the following spells are different from your standard cantrips. they are rare cantrips. spellcasters that gain access to all 0-level spells at 1st level do not gain access to rare cantrips. a spellcaster gains access to rare cantrips only by uncovering their secrets in some other way. some are guarded by jealous mages, while others are lost in missing libraries or molder on forgotten scrolls.\\n\\nthese cantrips are not legal in pathfinder society play. note that penumbra was changed into the higher-level spell protective penumbra. the cantrip version is similar, but does not replace its higher-level counterpart.\"",
    "sections": [],
    "document": {
      "node_type": "document",
      "content": [
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "This spell strengthens the subject’s connection to the ground below, bolstering its defense against combat maneuvers. It gains a +2 insight bonus to its CMD to resist being moved or tripped and a +2 competence bonus on all Acrobatics checks made to balance or remain standing on earth, sand, stone, or a similar rocky substance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "Note from Jason Bulmahn",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": ": The following spells are different from your standard cantrips. They are rare cantrips. Spellcasters that gain access to all 0-level spells at 1st level do not gain access to rare cantrips. A spellcaster gains access to rare cantrips only by uncovering their secrets in some other way. Some are guarded by jealous mages, while others are lost in missing libraries or molder on forgotten scrolls."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "These cantrips are not legal in Pathfinder Society play. Note that "
            },
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "penumbra",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": " was changed into the higher-level spell "
            },
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "protective penumbra",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": ". The cantrip version is similar, but does not replace its higher-level counterpart."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
